  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Facts: out, from the phone to ROS",
      "items": [
        "The page sends JSON over its one WebSocket; deliver() hands it on only while that link is the current phone (wsserver.py 212–218).",
        "parse() keeps the known fields of each message type and clamps every number (protocol.py 121–240); anything else is dropped with a warning.",
        "text() publishes standard types where they exist (Imu, Float32, BatteryState) and JSON in a String otherwise; IMU at most 60 Hz, faces 10 Hz, vision MAX_SEE_RATE (bridge_node.py 247–302).",
        "A face's familiar number goes out only while familiar is asked and allowed; otherwise the bridge sets it to null (bridge_node.py 292)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Facts: in, from ROS to the phone",
      "items": [
        "One subscription per in-topic; each goes through out() and a protocol maker that checks and clamps it before it is sent (bridge_node.py 88–101, 122–128).",
        "server.send() gives the phone the message and every mirror a copy (wsserver.py 184–188): diagram 09.",
        "Programs: omi_assist (tiles, the follower, reminders), guardian_node (the Desk Guardian, which also drives the Thymio: cmd_vel out, prox/ground in) and any program; they use only these topics (omi_assist.py 40–48, guardian_node.py 59–73). The setup page's tests publish on the same topics (bridge_node.py 109–113)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Held back from ROS",
      "items": [
        "Pictures: no topic carries a frame. A frame the person shows (Zeigen) goes to the setup page and to loopback mirrors only, and only while showing is allowed (bridge_node.py 338–342).",
        "The screen report goes to the mirrors, not to ROS (bridge_node.py 335–337). The text read aloud stays on the phone: read/result carries counts (contract.py 43).",
        "The location stays on the phone's screen: sensor_report() has no field for it (protocol.py 259–280)."
      ]
    }
  ]
